  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "roomba e5 wont charge properly, sometimes it does sometimes it doesnt"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Intermittent charging on a Roomba E5 is often caused by dirty charging contacts or issues with the power supply rather than a major internal fault. The most common culprits are oxidised metal pads on either the robot or the dock, or a loose wall outlet connection. To help narrow this down, please switch off and unplug the vacuum and dock, then gently wipe the gold charging contacts on both the robot and the dock with a dry cloth to remove any dust or residue. Also ensure the power cable is firmly plugged into both the dock and the wall socket. Let me know if it charges consistently after cleaning the contacts."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok i cleaned the contacts on the dock and the robot, they were grubby. it's charged every night for 4 days now, no error. is that it?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, that’s absolutely it! It sounds like cleaning those contacts has resolved the issue completely. To keep it running smoothly, just give those charging points a quick wipe with a dry cloth once or twice a year to prevent grime from building up again. I’m glad to hear your Roomba is back on track—is there anything else I can help you with today?"
  }
 ],
